Per-video frame clustering for Paxos2025 cleaned videos, used by MILVideoDatasetCluster (--cluster_sample).

extract_features.py: pretrained DINOv3 ViT-L CLS (224px) for every frame -> frame_clusters/features/<stem>.npy
train_contrastive.py: short InfoNCE on those features (port of retina_video_umap/train_contrastive.py); positives within
5 frames, negatives >= 30 frames apart (cleaned-video frame indices) -> frame_clusters/contrastive/
cluster_frames.py: k=32 cosine k-means per video -> frame_clusters/clusters/<stem>.json
({"num_frames", "k", "clusters", "medoids"}, clusters ordered by medoid frame)
vis_cluster_samples.py: image grid of the 32 cluster-sampled frames for random videos

Training: random frame per cluster each epoch, validation: medoids. Since 2026-10-20 random-segment sampling is the
default (same results, also works with Paxos2020).
